    "text": "An aqueous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi></math> solution of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> has a molality of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The molarity of the solution in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>molL</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is____.(The Nearest integer)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>74</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>]</mo></math>"
